# Line endings, and this is not a style preference.
#
# These files are executed by a POSIX shell: on a GitHub runner, inside WSL2 against a
# checkout on /mnt/c, and in a container. Written from Windows they get CRLF, and bash then
# fails with `$'\r': command not found` on line after line and dies at the first `for ... do`.
#
# It failed loudly rather than quietly - a CRLF `scripts/preflight.sh` reports failure, it
# does not report a green gate that ran nothing. But it failed on exactly the path
# CONTRIBUTING.md tells a Windows contributor to use, which is the path the gate exists for.
#
# tests/fast/test_preflight.py checks the bytes as well, because a .gitattributes only
# governs checkouts made after it was added.
*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
